<p style=3D"font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-a=
lign: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><font style=3D"font-family: Times New Ro=
man, Times, Serif"><b>3.1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&n=
bsp;&nbsp;</b></font><b><u>Access.</u></b>
From and after the Effective Date through the Closing Date, Buyer, personal=
ly or through its authorized agents or representatives,
shall be entitled, upon reasonable advance notice to Seller, to enter upon =
the Property and to make such investigations, including
appraisals, tenant interviews, engineering studies, interviews of governmen=
tal and quasi-governmental officials, soil tests, environmental
studies and underwriting analyses, as Buyer deems reasonably necessary or a=
dvisable. Buyer shall have the right to conduct a Phase
I environmental site assessment, and, if desired, a Phase II environmental =
site assessment (including soils borings, soil sampling
and, if relevant, ground water testing, and invasive sampling of building m=
aterials with respect to the Property). Buyer=92s
activities at the Property shall be conducted in such a manner so as not to=
 unreasonably interfere with the rights of the Tenants
under the Leases. Buyer will coordinate all on-site inspections and any con=
tact with tenants of the Property with Seller. Seller
shall have the option to have a representative present at any and all such =
on-site inspections or interviews. Buyer hereby agrees
to indemnify and hold Seller harmless from any physical damages arising out=
 of inspections and/or investigations by Buyer or its
agents or independent contractors; provided, however, and notwithstanding t=
he foregoing, that Buyer shall not be liable for any
pre-existing conditions at the Property.</p>

